e claimed she was  the victim  of an abusive boyfriend he smacked me  around sometimes  he would grab me and shake me and she  says steven had raped her  on two occasions and that's why she was  afraid of him  the night she shot him she had never  told  anyone that before and he can't defend  himself  mary catherine insists she was  embarrassed to tell the police that  stephen had a history of violence toward  her  what would a jury believe  wow and david begneau joins us now david  i want to talk about that uh  alleged confession tape uh police say it  happened but the tape apparently went  blank  what happened to that tape and how did  it affect the outcome of the case  tony it's like the one question i kept  having leading up to that interview with  the investigators how is it possible  that you guys  did this and it was like listen we  didn't mean to there was feedback on the  tape we don't know what happened  there's a lot of questions we then asked  them like well did you try again did you  go back when did you realize that you  had feedback on the tape  but the bottom line is that could have  been that could have been the number one  key thing the prosecution needed at the  trial  so without it what ended up happening  and how did it influence the verdict  you'll hear tonight prime time  10 o'clock 9 central all right looking  forward to it david thank you very much  and as david mentioned you can watch us  report the case against mary catherine  higdon  on 48 hours suspicion tonight at 10 9  central here on cbs
 

